X-ANTENNAS:    Indoor Cylinder dipole of two 500 ml energy drink cans
SOAPBOX:       I had great fun with QRP and a Cylinder Dipole of 38 cm 
SOAPBOX:       This Antenna is made from two energy drink cans of 500 ml and a coil
SOAPBOX:       I made about 20 QSO's with a power of 3.6 watts to 360 milliwatt
SOAPBOX:       I made QSO's on 7 MHz (2),  14 MHz (6) and 21 MHz (13)
SOAPBOX:       I was surprised to have a QSO with N1KWF over a distance of 3500 miles
SOAPBOX:       3 of the QSO's were more than 1000 Miles per Watt QSO's (hi)
SOAPBOX:       Not bad for an indoor antenna with a lenght of 15 inches at a hight of 4 meters
SOAPBOX:       The cylinder dipole puts out a strong signal and is very quiet on receive.
SOAPBOX:       For more info Google with --> PA1B cylinder dipole
SOAPBOX:       Thanks for the activity in the contest so I could test the indoor Cylinder Dipole
